---
/**
 * Demo: Core Web Vitals / PageSpeed plan for management.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { loadPageSeo } from '../../lib/seo';

const homeSeo = loadPageSeo('home');
const seo = {
  ...homeSeo,
  title: 'Core Web Vitals plan | Connect Group Astro demo',
  description:
    'How PageSpeed and Core Web Vitals are managed in the WordPress → Astro static migration.',
  canonical: 'https://connectgroup.co/demo/performance/',
  robots: 'noindex, follow',
};
---

<BaseLayout seo={seo}>
  <main class="perf">
    <p><a href="/demo/">← Demo hub</a></p>
    <h1>PageSpeed & Core Web Vitals</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Static Astro removes PHP/WordPress from the request path. Biggest CWV gains come when we
      stop shipping the full Elementor CSS/JS stack (Phase 4 rebuild), not from hosting alone.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>What we measure</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Metric</th>
            <th>Meaning</th>
            <th>Our plan</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>LCP</strong></td>
            <td>Largest Contentful Paint (hero loads fast)</td>
            <td>Local hero image, preload, compress to WebP/AVIF, CDN</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>INP</strong></td>
            <td>Interaction delay (menus, tabs, forms)</td>
            <td>Drop jQuery/Elementor JS; small Astro islands only where needed</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>CLS</strong></td>
            <td>Layout shift</td>
            <td>Width/height on images; fonts with fallback; no late-injected banners</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Phase vs performance</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Phase</th>
            <th>What ships</th>
            <th>Expected CWV impact</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Phase 1 (now)</td>
            <td>Elementor HTML + CSS/JS mirror, assets on Astro static host</td>
            <td>
              Better TTFB (no PHP). LCP/INP still limited by heavy Elementor bundle —
              acceptable for visual demo, not final score target
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Phase 2</td>
            <td>Replace CF7 / plugin scripts</td>
            <td>Fewer third-party scripts → better INP</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Phase 3</td>
            <td>Shared Header/Footer components</td>
            <td>Less duplicate CSS/JS across pages</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Phase 4</td>
            <td>Rebuild homepage sections in Astro</td>
            <td>
              <strong>Main CWV win</strong> — lean HTML/CSS, image optimization, minimal JS
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Phase 5</td>
            <td>CDN cutover</td>
            <td>Edge caching + HTTP/2/3 globally</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>How the team will manage speed</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Budgets:</strong> track Lighthouse / PageSpeed Insights on staging for `/`
          and top landings (P0 URLs).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Images:</strong> Astro <code>astro:assets</code> or pre-optimized WebP in
          <code>public/</code>; always set dimensions.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>JS:</strong> default zero; client islands only for mega-menu / carousel /
          form validation.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>CSS:</strong> critical CSS per template; remove Elementor ID-soup styles over
          time.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Third parties:</strong> load GTM/marketing tags after consent / deferred —
          audit Leadfeeder, ZoomInfo, Instagram.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Hosts:</strong> Cloudflare Pages / Netlify / Vercel static + CDN (same idea).
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Demo tip for managers</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Run PageSpeed on live WordPress vs this Astro mirror (TTFB usually improves).</li>
        <li>Explain we are not chasing a 95 Lighthouse on the Elementor dump.</li>
        <li>Show rebuilt path: YAML SEO + lean Astro sections = lasting CWV gains.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Full write-up: <code>docs/09-pagespeed-core-web-vitals.md</code>
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .perf {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Sans", "Segoe UI", system-ui, sans-serif;
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem 1.25rem 4rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: #0f172a;
  }
  .perf a {
    color: #1e3a8a;
  }
  h1 {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Serif", Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 1.85rem;
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0.75rem;
  }
  .lead {
    color: #475569;
  }
  section {
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  }
  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
  }
  th,
  td {
    border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
    padding: 0.55rem 0.65rem;
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  th {
    background: #f8fafc;
  }
  ul,
  ol {
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
  }
  li {
    margin-bottom: 0.45rem;
  }
  code {
    font-size: 0.86em;
    background: #f1f5f9;
    padding: 0.1em 0.35em;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }
</style>
